        "notes": "An immoveable, so the Irish forum applies the lex situs. Note the divergence a Spanish court would see: Spain applies Regulation (EU) 650/2012, which refers the whole succession to the law of the deceased's habitual residence. Ireland does not participate in that Regulation. The two fora can therefore reach the same asset by different routes, which is why the connecting factor is recorded rather than inferred."
